# The documentation site

`docs/` is a standalone Next.js 16 + Fumadocs app. It carries its own
`pnpm-workspace.yaml`, so a root `pnpm install` **ignores it**, and the root eslint config
ignores it too. Work on it from inside `docs/`:

```bash
cd docs && pnpm install && pnpm dev    # → http://localhost:3000
```

## Two generated inputs — do not hand-edit either

- `content/docs/reference/configuration.md` is generated by `pnpm run config:docs` **in
  the repo root**, and a drift test compares it byte for byte.
- `public/diagrams/*.svg` are copied from `../assets` by `scripts/sync-generated.mjs`,
  which `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build` run automatically. Edit `assets/<name>.svg` — both
  READMEs reference that path directly.

## Content

MDX under `content/docs/`, one `meta.json` per folder controlling order and titles.

Components available without importing: `Callout`, `Cards`/`Card`, `Steps`/`Step`,
`Tabs`/`Tab`, `Accordion(s)`, `Files`/`File`/`Folder`, `TypeTable` — all registered in
`components/mdx.tsx`. **A page that uses an unregistered component fails the build**,
which is the intended behaviour.

MDX parses bare `<word>` as JSX. Wrap things like `<rel>` and `<name>` in backticks, or
the build fails with an unclosed-tag error.

A fenced example containing fences needs a **longer** outer fence than any inner one.

## SEO

Every SEO surface lives in `lib/seo.tsx` and `lib/shared.ts`. Add a tag there, not in a
page. Verification tokens are optional and render **no tag at all** when unset — an empty
`content=""` reads as a failed claim rather than an absent one.
